  {
   "id": "OWj7CWyZmkkJ",
   "from": "Altuna Akalin",
   "author": "ab8277113f65c05e",
   "date": "2014-11-05T13:02:12Z",
   "subject": "Re: [methylkit_discussion] Re: invalid 'times' argument while creating gene object",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The problem here is the underscore &quot;_&quot; in chromosome names, by default read.transcript.features() removes the chromosome names with &quot;_&quot;. There are a bunch of such chromosome in human and mouse genome and possibly other genomes, normally we do not work on those chromosomes although they are part of the assembly. setting remove.unsual=FALSE when calling the function should resolve the issue.<div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Altuna</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Nov 5, 2014 at 1:58 PM, Kalyan K Pasumarthy <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">kaly...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Information about BED format is available at  <a href=\"http://genome.ucsc.edu/FAQ/FAQformat.html#format1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://genome.ucsc.edu/FAQ/FAQformat.html%23format1&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793233999485000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ENClaCfCtBuw3xSzVswOf\">http://genome.ucsc.edu/FAQ/FAQformat.html#format1</a> This may help you.</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Regards,<br>Kalyan<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"width:auto;height:30px;font-size:0px\"></td></tr><tr><td style=\"width:auto\"><div style=\"line-height:0\"><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"width:48px;line-height:1;vertical-align:top\" valign=\"top\" align=\"left\"><br></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td style=\"width:8px;font-size:0px\"><br></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td style=\"width:auto;height:48px;line-height:1;padding:0px;vertical-align:middle\" valign=\"middle\" align=\"left\"><br></td>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tbody>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</table>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\t</div></td></tr>\r\n\t\t\t<tr><td style=\"width:auto;height:20px;font-size:0px\"> </td></tr>\r\n\t\t</tbody>\r\n\t</table>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<br></div></div></div><div><div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On 5 November 2014 14:51, Saranya Sankaranarayanan <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sara...@umail.iu.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#0b5394\">Hi Kalyan,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#0b5394\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#0b5394\">Thanks a lot or your input. Could you give an insight as to why it is not accepting the first column as NW_? Is it mandatory for me to change the column 1 to chromosome numbers? </div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><span><br clear=\"all\"><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><font><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Sincerely,</span></font></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><font><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Saranya Sankaranarayanan</span></font></span></div><div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><font><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Master&#39;s Student, SoIC</span></font></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><font><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Indiana University</span></font></span></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n<br></span><div><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Nov 4, 2014 at 1:48 PM, Saranya Sankaranarayanan <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sara...@umail.iu.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Hi authors,<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">I am trying to pass a bed file as a gene object in methylkit and face the error :<br><br>&gt; library(methylKit)<br>&gt; gene.obj&lt;- read.transcript.features(&quot;Amel.bed&quot;)<br>Error in rep(1:nrow(ref), ref[, 10]) : invalid &#39;times&#39; argument<br><br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">I looked into the forum  where you have suggested that there might be some &#39;NA&#39; in the file and hence the error. As for this bedfile, everything looks okay. I am not sure if I am missing something. Could you please help me with this.<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">I had a gff3 file (ref_Amel_4.5_top_level.gff3) from (<a href=\"http://mirrors.vbi.vt.edu/mirrors/ftp.ncbi.nih.gov/genomes/Apis_mellifera/GFF/ref_Amel_4.5_top_level.gff3.gz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mirrors.vbi.vt.edu/mirrors/ftp.ncbi.nih.gov/genomes/Apis_mellifera/GFF/ref_Amel_4.5_top_level.gff3.gz&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793233999485000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1GDGreg_HmO5k28YxLTnvS\">http://mirrors.vbi.vt.edu/mirrors/ftp.ncbi.nih.gov/genomes/Apis_mellifera/GFF/ref_Amel_4.5_top_level.gff3.gz</a>)<br>which I converted using a python script gff3_to_bed_converter.py and got the 12 column bed file(Amel.bed)<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">I have attached all the files for your reference. Could you please help me with this?<br><br><br clear=\"all\"></div><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><font><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Sincerely,</span></font></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><font><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Saranya Sankaranarayanan</span></font></span></div><div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><font><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Master&#39;s Student, SoIC</span></font></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><font><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Indiana University</span></font></span></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote></div><br></div></div></div><div><div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;methylkit_discussion&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">methylkit_discus...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">methylkit_...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/methylkit_discussion\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/methylkit_discussion&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793233999485000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1SHlmVpSZnXIMiVjal-1LW\">http://groups.google.com/group/methylkit_discussion</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793233999485000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1kULf0bcC_OtAjGQYpz17d\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</div></div></blockquote></div><br></div></div></div><div><div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;methylkit_discussion&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">methylkit_discus...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">methylkit_...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/methylkit_discussion\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US